                "Assessments": {
                  "value": "",
                  "source": "commons-categories",
                  "hidden": ""
                },
                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "Flow diagram showing how participants move through the four stages of a two-group parallel randomized trial: enrollment, allocation, follow-up and analysis. It is redrawn from the CONSORT 2010 flow diagram template and keeps the template's wording and spellings (\"Enrollment\", \"Randomized\", \"Analysed\"). Both arms read \"Allocated to intervention\" because the template does not name the arms; in a controlled trial, one of them is the comparator. The counts are blank (\"n= \") so that a trial report can fill them in.\n<p>Enrollment: Assessed for eligibility (n= ); Excluded (n= ): Not meeting inclusion criteria (n= ), Declined to participate (n= ), Other reasons (n= ); Randomized (n= ).\nAllocation (each arm): Allocated to intervention (n= ): Received allocated intervention (n= ), Did not receive allocated intervention (give reasons) (n= ).\nFollow-Up (each arm): Lost to follow-up (give reasons) (n= ); Discontinued intervention (give reasons) (n= ).\nAnalysis (each arm): Analysed (n= ): Excluded from analysis (give reasons) (n= ).\n</p>\nCONSORT 2025 (Hopewell et al. 2025) changed the diagram. Follow-up now lists \"Discontinued intervention\" first and counts \"Lost to follow-up for primary outcome\", and analysis reads \"Analysed for primary outcome\". This file shows the 2010 version.",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
                "DateTimeOriginal": {
                  "value": "2026-10-18",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
                "Credit": {
                  "value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>, based on the CONSORT 2010 flow diagram (Schulz, Altman and Moher 2010, Figure 1)",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
